t). Previously, the default was Version 2. The sample OData back-end service is available for developers to use during development and testing, and to evaluate how delta tokens are handled in test applications.   See Using the Mobile Sample OData ESPM\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-25\nValid as Of: 2024-04-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3154 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Test back-end connectivity (Allowed Paths)\nDescription: (Version: 2403) You can now test back-end connectivity more easily when Allowed Paths is configured for a destination. When configured, and you select Testing an OData Destination or  Testing Destinations in a Browser, you are prompted to select the path. For example, a path for Version 2 and one for Version 4. If Allowed Paths is not configured for the destination, you are not prompted. Previously, you needed to enter the specific path manually when tested connectivity.  See:    Testing OData Destinations      Testing Destinations in a Browser    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3155 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Web application option removed\nDescription: (Version: 2403) The Web application option has been removed from the Create New App and New dialogs. The Web app template was used for applications that run in a Web browser. Existing Web apps continue to be supported, and other development options are now available for Web apps.  See Creating an Application\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-25\nValid as Of: 2024-04-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3156 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Apps\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Web & Mobile\nDescription:   Accessibility improvements to the UI elements.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-09\nValid as Of: 2024-04-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3157 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Selected models from GCP Vertex AI are supported.  For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-08\nValid as Of: 2024-04-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3158 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Selected models from GCP Vertex AI are supported.  For more information, see Models and Scenarios in the Generative AI Hub.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-08\nValid as Of: 2024-04-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3159 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: For generative models that support it, a 32k context window is available.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-08\nValid as Of: 2024-04-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3160 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Workspaces\nDescription: Connection creation in Workspaces through x.509 certificates is supported.  For more information, see Create a Service Key in SAP AI Core", "Action: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-08\nValid as Of: 2024-04-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3160 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Workspaces\nDescription: Connection creation in Workspaces through x.509 certificates is supported.  For more information, see Create a Service Key in SAP AI Core and Add Connection to SAP AI Core.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-08\nValid as Of: 2024-04-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 41 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 2.40.0\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 2 has been updated from version 2.39.0 to 2.40.0. Updated components:       Tomcat 10 is updated from version 10.1.44 to 10.1.45      com.sap.core.connectivity.jco is updated from version 5.0.1 to 5.0.2      com.sap.cloud.security.xsuaa is updated from version 3.6.3 to 3.6.4    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-20\nValid as Of: 2025-10-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 42 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Administrator's Guide\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Other\nTitle: Updated Shared Responsibility Model\nDescription: In alignment with the learning journey for administrators, we've updated the Shared Responsibility Model Between You and SAP.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-25\nValid as Of: 2025-09-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 43 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Content Displayed on SAP Mobile Start\nDescription: We’ve corrected the unintended behavior of content in the different view modes of Groups and Spaces and Pages when using SAP Mobile Start.   Now when accessing a site on SAP Mobile Start, only the content that is relevant to the selected view mode is displayed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-16\nValid as Of: 2025-09-29\nVersion: 2509A\n\n--- Record 44 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Content Displayed on SAP Mobile Start\nDescription: We’ve corrected the unintended behavior of content in the different view modes of Groups and Spaces and Pages when using SAP Mobile Start.   Now when accessing a site on SAP Mobile Start, only the content that is relevant to the selected view mode is displayed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-16\nValid as Of: 2025-09-29\nVersion: 2509A\n\n--- Record 45 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: New Type of User for Agent Registration\nDescription: For increased security, you now use a new type of user called an Agent user to register a Data Services Agent. For more information, see User Administration and Registering an Agent in the Web Interface.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-08\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: 2509\n\n--- Record 46 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: \"DSOD\" No Longer Appears in the URL for SAP Cloud Integration for data services\nDescription: \"DSOD\" has been removed from the URL for SAP Cloud Integration for data services on SAP BTP, Kyma runtime. The following documentation has been modified:  Finish Setting Up a Standard User  Creating a Client to Use Web Services  Accessing the WSDL File  Agent Diagnostics Available via the Command Line  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-19\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: 2509\n\n--- Record 47 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Announcement: User Interface Supporting Migration from the Neo Environment to Kyma Runtime\nDescription: In the Administration user interface of SAP Cloud Integration for data services, an Off-Neo Migration workflow is being rolled out. Once enabled for you, the workflow guides you through the process of migrating from the Neo environment to the Kyma runtime. You will receive an SAP Customer Communication with details about the availability of this workflow in your system. The Tenant Migration Guide and in particular UI Location and Visibility of the Tenant Migration Request contain helpful information about the workflow.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-09\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: 2509\n\n--- Record 48 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Documentation update only: Compilation of Security Recommendations\nDescription: Security-related recommendations that appear in various places within the SAP Cloud Integration for data services documentation set have been compiled into an easily readable table in Security Recommendations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-18\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: 2509\n\n--- Record 49 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Documentation update only: Do Not Use Standard Users for Web Services\nDescription: User Administration has been updated to reflect that standard users should not be used for web services.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed", " Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-18\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: 2509\n\n--- Record 49 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Documentation update only: Do Not Use Standard Users for Web Services\nDescription: User Administration has been updated to reflect that standard users should not be used for web services.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-19\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: 2509\n\n--- Record 50 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Documentation update only: End of Support for Azure Data Lake Storage Gen1\nDescription: Due to Microsoft's having ended support of Azure Data Lake Storage Gen1 in early 2024, SAP Cloud Integration for data services will end support of Gen1 in an early 2026 release. We recommend, as does Microsoft, that you use ADLS Gen2 instead. For more information, see Moving from ADLS Gen1 to Gen2.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-09\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: 2509\n\n", "--- Record 1311 ---\nComponent: Forms Service by Adobe\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: REST API - New Output Types\nDescription: The SAP Forms service REST API now supports the following additional output types:  • CAB  • DPL  • IPL  • PCL  • PS  • TPCL  • ZPL  For more information, see Render Additional Output Types.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-02-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1312 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Additional worker node pools\nDescription: We have added a new configurable parameter, Additional Worker Node Pools (additionalWorkerNodePools). Adding a customized worker node pool to your Kyma runtime enables you to introduce worker nodes optimized and reserved for your particular workload requirements.  For more information, see Provisioning and Updating Parameters in the Kyma Environment.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-26\nValid as Of: 2025-02-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1313 ---\nComponent: Process Visibility Capability\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Step Execution Details in Process Path\nDescription: You can now view step-level details for every execution of step that runs in loops.   See Gain Visibility Using Process Workspace.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-26\nValid as Of: 2025-02-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1314 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Add Dependent Project Processes to Visibility Scenario\nDescription: You can now gain visibility on processes added from dependent projects in your visibility scenario.See Add Process.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-26\nValid as Of: 2025-02-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1315 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Step Execution Details in Process Path\nDescription: You can now view step-level details for every execution of step that runs in loops.See Gain Visibility Using Process Workspace.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-26\nValid as Of: 2025-02-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1316 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Central store-based provisioning\nDescription: You can enable central store-based provisioning to immediately provision updates related to user assignments in application-specific groups between the Local Identity Directory and your selected target systems.  For more information, see Enable or Disable Central Store-Based Provisioning and Central Store-Based Provisioning.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-25\nValid as Of: 2025-02-25\nVersion: 27494\n\n--- Record 1317 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Certificate Renewal\nDescription: Identity Authentication can update automatically the expired encryption certificate, and the SAML 2.0 certificate during the first sign in attempt that fails due to the expired certificate. The metadata URL must be provided. See Configure SAML 2.0 Service Provider.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-25\nValid as Of: 2025-02-25\nVersion: 27494\n\n--- Record 1318 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Group mapping changes\nDescription: The default transformations of SAP S/4 HANA Cloud are changed to support the provisioning of application-specific groups.  For more information, see:  SAP S/4 HANA Cloud (Source)  SAP S/4 HANA Cloud (Target)  SAP S/4 HANA Cloud (Proxy)  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-25\nValid as Of: 2025-02-25\nVersion: 27494\n\n--- Record 1319 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Group Provisioning\nDescription: You can enable or disable provisioning of every update in an application specific group to a target system. See Enable or Disable Central Store-Based Provisioning.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-25\nValid as Of: 2025-02-25\nVersion: 27494\n\n--- Record 1320 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Increased Number of API Permission Groups Allowed\nDescription: API permission groups enable you to expose APIs to other Cloud Identity Services applications. With this release, we have increased the number of API permission groups you can create from 20 to 50.  For more information, see Provide APIs for Consumption by Other Applications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-25", ",Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Increased Number of API Permission Groups Allowed\nDescription: API permission groups enable you to expose APIs to other Cloud Identity Services applications. With this release, we have increased the number of API permission groups you can create from 20 to 50.  For more information, see Provide APIs for Consumption by Other Applications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-25\nValid as Of: 2025-02-25\nVersion: 27494\n\n", "--- Record 3681 ---\nComponent: SAP Excise Tax Management\nEnvironment: Other\nTitle: Inventory Settlement Report\nDescription: The Inventory Settlement report for alcohol (DEALC_1279_SAP) has been updated to include a new filter Tax-Dependent Material Group. Once the report has been generated, you can use this filter in the report to view the data for specific tax-dependent material groups.  Note  In order for this feature to work correctly, you must perform the following actions:    Maintain the tax-dependent material groups for your master data in the Edit Excise Tax Material Master Data app.      Import the latest SAP Analytics Cloud content for the standard reports from the content network into your SAP Analytics Cloud tenant. For more information, see Importing SAP Analytics Cloud Content for Legal Reports.      Update custom reports (if you have any) with the new changes seen in the standard reports. We recommend that you implement your customizations again on top of the latest SAP Analytics Cloud content for the standard reports.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-01-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3682 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Vertical Layout in Process Editor\nDescription: The vertical layout is available in the following regions:      Australia (Sydney)(cf-ap10)      US Central (IA) (cf-us30)      Europe (Frankfurt) (cf-eu11)      Japan (Tokyo) (cf-jp10)      See the documentation marked as early adopter version at: Business Process Projects.  These are some of the advantages that the new layout offers you:      To move process steps that have already been connected to the process, you simply select the step and drag and drop them.      You can access embedded help using the question mark button (?). In the Help Panel, you can navigate between the help for UI elements, the embedded What's New, and the Guided Tours.      If, for example, the outcome of an approval step in your process is “reject”, you can insert a go-to step and send users back to a previous step asking them to rework their entries.  See Use Cases for Custom Variables.      The side panel is wider and easier to work with. You can close it to save space. To display process information again, use the toggle button in the side panel.      You can select the next step to insert in your process from the smart menu.  See step 6 in Create a Business Process.      Steps with more than one flow are visualized as a group. You can collapse groups to get a better overview of the whole process.      The process is always valid, there are no more dangling ends. If you add a new step, for example, an approval form, all output paths are connected. You do not have to connect, for example, the Reject outcome to the process anymore.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Restricted Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-21\nValid as Of: 2024-01-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3683 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Breaking change - cluster region mandatory for enabling Kyma runtime\nDescription: As we announced in this release note, the Region parameter is mandatory for provisioning Kyma runtime in your cluster. The change affects all the available plans in the Kyma environment except for the Trial plan. When you enable your Kyma runtime, choose the region from the menu list in the SAP BTP cockpit or provide a cluster region name in the SAP BTP command line interface.  For more information, read the Region input parameter required for provisioning SAP BTP, Kyma runtime in your cluster blog post.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-21\nValid as Of: 2024-01-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3684 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integrating SAP S/4HANA with Google Workspace Using SAP Document Management Service\nDescription: With this release, we've changed the destination configuration. The following properties have been replaced:    Old Property  New Property        Authentication: NoAuthentication  OAuth2ClientCredentials      Additional Property: google.client_id    Standard Configuration: Client ID      Additional Property:google.private_key  Standard Configuration: Client Secret      Additional Property:google.token_uri   Standard Configuration: Token Service URL    Action: If you're an existing user,, it's required to migrate your settings to the new setup. The updates are designed to enhance the experience for new implementations, ensuring a seamless and optimized setup.  For more information about creating destinations, see Creating HTTP Destinations.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-04\nValid as Of: 2024-01-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3685 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Identity Authentication has been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-04\nValid as Of: 2024-01-04\nVersion: 25446\n\n--- Record 3686 ---\nComponent: Documentation\nEnvironme